          "email": "ynachum@amazon.com",
          "date": "2026-10-05 14:48:16.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20790 efalnd: Free Rx buffer on lnet_parse error",
        "message": "LU-20790 efalnd: Free Rx buffer on lnet_parse error\n\nlnet_parse() can return an error and in that case LNet doesn't call the\nLND receive callback, which means the Rx buffer is never released and is\nleaked together with its RQ slot.\n\nReturn the lnet_parse() return code, so that handle Rx flow will release\nthe buffer on error. LNet only returns a negative value before taking\nownership of the buffer, so there is no risk of releasing a buffer that\nLNet owns.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 0c773016d837 (\"LU-18977 efalnd: Introduce AWS EFA Lustre network driver\")\nSigned-off-by: Yonatan Nachum <ynachum@amazon.com>\nSigned-off-by: Zanhua Huang <zanhua@amazon.com>\nChange-Id: I704c413fe9959ed32693c3d5d21e7a9c654f0be6\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
